# Supervised paths — changes here require a human in the loop.
#
# Not "do not touch". These paths are in bounds for agent work; they are out
# of bounds for agent work that MERGES ITSELF. The distinction is the whole
# point: everything else in this repository has an oracle that can fail a bad
# change without a person present (see docs/ORACLES.md). These paths do not.
# The only thing standing between a plausible-looking change here and main is
# somebody opening the page and looking at it.
#
# Enforced by scripts/check-supervised-paths.sh, not by policy. A rule that
# lives only in a document is a rule an unattended runner never reads.
#
# One glob per line, matched against repo-relative paths. Blank lines and
# lines beginning with # are ignored.

# The entire web frontend. index.html and spectator.html carry the board
# rendering, move input, challenge flow, and live-update handling inline.
# There is no rendering test, no DOM assertion, no interaction test, and no
# screenshot diff. internal/web/static_derivation_incomplete_guard_test.go
# greps these files for one string; that is a tripwire for a single known
# regression, not coverage.
web/static/*

# OAuth client metadata is served to third parties and mis-editing it breaks
# login for everyone, in a way no test here would catch.
web/static/client-metadata.json
